  "faqs": [
    {
      "q": "What dew point does a WRD dryer deliver?",
      "a": "WRD dryers deliver a +3 °C pressure dew point and hold it at varying load using a thermostatic expansion valve and hot gas bypass valve."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I size a refrigerated dryer for my compressor?",
      "a": "Divide your compressor's actual capacity by the product of the four correction factors for inlet temperature, ambient temperature, inlet pressure and dew point. Then choose the WRD model at or above that nominal capacity. The sizing tool on this page does the calculation for you."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which models run on single-phase power?",
      "a": "Models with an S suffix (WRD 20 S to WRD 250 S) run on 230 V single phase. T models from WRD 300 T upward run on three-phase supply."
    },
    {
      "q": "Is a water-cooled condenser available?",
      "a": "Yes. WRD 600 T and larger are offered with air- or water-cooled condensers."
    }
  ],
